notes={
1:('Branching meadow food web shows food to consumer, solar input to plant and outgoing heat from plant and every consumer. No energy-return cycle or universal numerical transfer efficiency is pictured. Grass/grasshopper/frog/stork and grass/mouse/stork are coherent representative paths. Decomposers and actual population dynamics remain whole-case/text work; this overview never purports to depict the entire whole competence.','At 360 the organisms and all arrow directions stay distinct; Nahrung/Wärme are small auxiliary labels, readable but not required to infer direction from the large arrows. At 680 those labels and every branch are clear.'),
2:('Two conditional dry/wet structural examples distinguish thicker cuticle and sheltered pore from broad thinner leaf. Leaf magnifications remain connected to actual leaves. Blue arrows leave pores and rise from soil towards roots; no inverted transpiration. Tissue is schematic rather than a named microscopic species claim. No claim all wet/dry species share these exact traits.','At 360 both blade shapes, thick/thin upper layers and outward pore arrows remain visible. Trocken/Feucht stay readable. At 680 pore opening, cuticle and root-uptake directions are fully separable.'),
3:('Compact dense-furred small-ear cold example is contrasted with large thin ears and ear blood vessels in the warm example. Body heat sources and outward heat icons separate physiological heat flow from morphological form; no exception-free Allen/Bergmann or universal numerical claim.','Both ear/body contrasts, thermoregulation circles and Kalt/Warm remain clear at 360; the vascular inset is recognisable. All three detail classes are distinctly readable at 680.'),
4:('Green prey maximum precedes orange predator maximum. Rabbit green arrow ends on green peak; lynx orange arrow ends on orange peak. Bestand is vertical and Zeit horizontal. Modell and external weather arrow signal idealisation and boundary conditions rather than observed census data. Whole common logistic cases and separate BY-EA LV extension were independently read before image context. This schematic is not a universal source-course obligation.','At 360 both animals, differently coloured phase-shifted curves, their correctly assigned arrows, axis labels and external influence are clear. At 680 the lynx-to-orange mapping is unequivocal. Earlier v1 captures were not viewed and receive no approval.'),
5:('Wall bank and vegetated habitat bank contrast a management option, habitat structure and monitoring. Fish remain present on the wall side; the image does not falsely say urban banks support no life. Habitat protection arrows and an observing person/checklist show mechanisms and subsequent checking, without guaranteed success.','At 360 bank structure, fish/vegetation contrast and the observing person/checklist remain recognisable; Schutz/Ufer/Kontrolle are readable. At 680 habitat features and monitoring are clear.'),
6:('Daily torpor is drawn as one lowered metabolic interval against day/night, seasonal hibernation as longer low baseline with several brief arousal peaks and subsequent spring rise. Stoffwechsel names the ordinate quantity and Zeit labels horizontal time. Temperature symbols show reduction, not a universal exact temperature or continuous ordinary sleep.','At 360 both daily/seasonal time strips and reduced metabolism/arousal peaks remain visible and primary Torpor/Winterschlaf labels readable. At 680 chart axes and recurrent peaks are clear; no minute numerical text is required.'),
7:('Resource demand footprint contains food, mobility and housing; the opposing productive landscape represents biocapacity. The comparison arrow does not draw a factual equality or reduce footprint to CO2 alone. Bike/food choices are illustrative, not quantified proven offsets. Whole per-person/aggregate arithmetic and indicator limits remain in the independently read cases.','At 360 footprint categories, landscape and Bedarf/Biokapazität remain distinct; at 680 all category icons and the comparison are clear. No small numbers must be read.'),
8:('Real field procedure is represented by meadow quadrats/transect, observation tools and subsequent documentation. Empty notebook/table cells do not pretend that actual personal field data or learner evidence already exists. The acting writer faces the working notebook; no upside-down observer-only entries are drawn.','At 360 quadrats, observer, arrow to documentation and large empty species table remain distinct; at 680 field tools and notebook orientation are clear. No unreadable synthetic readings are required.'),
11:('Many offspring in a disturbed rabbit example versus fewer dependent raptor young and stable habitat is explicitly labelled Modell. Bidirectional gradient arrow represents the r/K continuum; parental presence on both sides avoids claiming r species have no care. This is a comparative idealisation, not an exhaustive species classification or moral ranking.','At 360 offspring-number contrast, disturbed/stable setting and r/K model continuum remain clear. Viele/Wenige/Modell and r/K are readable; at 680 offspring and parental context are unmistakable.'),
13:('Courtship, territorial signalling and cooperative parental care are distinct behaviours. Energy-up icons depict costs alongside possible offspring benefits. Heart is a friendly courtship symbol, not asserted evolutionary intent; the actual cases explicitly reject intention and unsupported kin-selection certainty. No displayed data prove a historical adaptive story.','At 360 all three behaviours, energy-cost/offspring icons and Balz/Revier/Kooperation remain distinguishable; at 680 whole three-part comparison is clear. Small bird details are decorative rather than assessment text.'),
14:('Upward habitat shift and finite mountain summit illustrate conditional spatial limits. Time/flower-pollinator paired symbols with dashed relation/question express possible altered timing, not a guaranteed extinction, measured climate attribution or every species moving uniformly.','At 360 warming, ascending range and flower/pollinator timing question remain visible; primary Klima/Lebensraum/Zeit labels are readable. At 680 range boundaries and changed interaction symbols are clear.'),
16:('Wetland circles show water service, buffering, reeds as raw material and recreation. Money versus biodiversity scales represent consideration of economic and nonmonetary ecological values, not factual numerical equivalence. No currency amount, guaranteed potable water or automatic compensation is claimed. Notebook faces the actor without reversed mandatory text.','At 360 the four service categories, money/ecology sides and Werte labels remain clear; at 680 all service icons and valuation contrast are readable. Whole quantitative examples and double-counting/unknown-value caveats remain independently approved text/cases.')}
out=[]; files=[]
